   131→ * @remark The polynomial should have FIELD_ELEMENTS_PER_BLOB coefficients. Only the lower half of
   132→ * the extended polynomial is supplied because the upper half is assumed to be zero.
   133→ *
   134→ * @remark The configuration of this protocol currently (May 2025) assumes r=l and n=2r. This may
   135→ * result in some optimizations, not particularly suited for r being much different to l. However,
   136→ * the code is supposed to work also for l=1, which is the case of FK20 regular (single) proofs.
   137→ */
